results.evidence:
In `frontend/src/scenes/settings/organization/InviteModal.tsx`:
```tsx
onBlur={() => checkInviteEmail(index)}
...
{invitesToSend[index]?.emailError && (
    <div className="text-danger text-xs mt-1" role="alert">
        {invitesToSend[index].emailError === 'already_member'
            ? 'This email belongs to an organization member. Change it or remove the row.'
            : 'Enter a valid email address.'}
    </div>
)}
```
and in `frontend/src/scenes/settings/organization/inviteLogic.ts`:
```ts
const alreadyMember = await api.create<boolean>(
    `api/organizations/${organizationId}/invites/check_email/`,
    { email }
)
...
actions.updateInviteAtIndex(
    {
        isValid: !alreadyMember,
        emailError: alreadyMember ? 'already_member' : undefined,
        isCheckingEmail: false,
    },
    index
)
```

In `posthog/api/organization_invite.py`:
```python
        if OrganizationMembership.objects.filter(
            organization_id=self.context["organization_id"], user__email__iexact=email
        ).exists():
            raise exceptions.ValidationError(
                "A user with this email address already belongs to the organization.", code="already_member"
            )
```
Moving the membership validation into `validate_target_email` causes DRF to evaluate all rows upfront in `is_valid()` before `create()` runs for any row, aborting the bulk request before any invite is created or emailed.

In `frontend/src/scenes/settings/organization/inviteLogic.ts`:
```ts
        inviteTeamMembersFailure: ({ errorObject }): void => {
            if (errorObject?.code === 'already_member') {
                values.invitesToSend.forEach((invite, index) => {
                    if (invite.target_email) {
                        actions.checkInviteEmail(index)
                    }
                })
            }
        },
```
When the server rejects with `code === 'already_member'`, `inviteTeamMembersFailure` re-evaluates the invite rows via `checkInviteEmail(index)`, flagging the offending row with `emailError: 'already_member'`.
